-- title:
--   Components of the special fibre counted by minimal primes of varpi
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure, and $j \in F$ with $j \neq 0$. Write $A_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `chartAlgFin R F j` for the subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over $R[j]$ and $A_{\mathrm{inf}} =$ `chartAlgInf R F j` for the subalgebra of elements integral over $R[j^{-1}]$; the two-chart integral model $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel R F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the pushout in schemes of the two maps `fFin`, `fInf` from the middle chart to $\operatorname{Spec} A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $\operatorname{Spec} A_{\mathrm{inf}}$, and `toBase R F j : X ⟶ Spec R` is the morphism obtained from the structure maps $\operatorname{Spec} A_{\mathrm{fin}} \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ and $\operatorname{Spec} A_{\mathrm{inf}} \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ by the universal property. Fix $\varpi \in R$ and a field $\kappa$ with an $R$-algebra structure such that $\operatorname{algebraMap} R\ \kappa$ is surjective with kernel the ideal $(\varpi)$. Assume that no minimal prime of the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$ in $A_{\mathrm{inf}}$ contains $j^{-1}$ (viewed as the element `jInvChartInf R F j` of $A_{\mathrm{inf}}$). Then the set of irreducible components of the underlying topological space of the fibre product of `toBase R F j` with $\operatorname{Spec} \kappa \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ has the same cardinality, measured by `Set.ncard`, as the set of minimal primes of the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$ in $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$.
--
--   This counts the irreducible components of the special fibre $X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} \kappa$ of a two-chart integral model purely in terms of the minimal primes above $\varpi$ in the $j$-finite chart, the hypothesis on $A_{\mathrm{inf}}$ ensuring that every component has its generic point in that chart. It is used in the analysis of the mod-$p$ fibre of the model of $X_1(p)$, in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_opens_hom_mapsTo_irreducibleComponents_pullback_modelTo_zmod_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_opens_hom_mapsTo_irreducibleComponents_pullback_modelTo_zmod_x1_mul) and [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_pair_irreducibleComponents_pullback_modelTo_zmod_eq_or_eq_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_pair_irreducibleComponents_pullback_modelTo_zmod_eq_or_eq_x1_mul).
